ROWS=[('10.1021/acsami.8b15629', '13787486-am8b15629_si_001.pdf', '13787486', 'SI sections1–6, TableS1, TableS4 block headings; PDFp18 visually checked', 'Protein-crystallization seeds include rectangle and rolled tubes. Methods give tube diameters8/11/22nm,100nm length and2nm wall; FigS3 gives70x100nm rectangle, whereas TableS1 says110nm length. Sequence blocks label12nm rectangle/tube side chains, conflicting with11nm experimental label; PDFp18 visually confirms12nm. Retain ambiguity rather than normalize dimensions. TableS4 has8nm and22nm tube lists plus side-chain replacements, not yet reconciled to complete variant recipes. Protein concentrations and incubation times are conditions; blank/M13/M13rs controls are not new origami cores. Exact scaffold identity, parent/native sources, all row mappings and narrow eligibility remain pending.'), ('10.1021/acsami.8b19153', '13786913-am8b19153_si_001.pdf', '13786913', 'SI Materials p2; TableS2 and methods pp5–6; FigS6–10; PDFp6 visually checked', 'Chiral plasmonic sensor uses core staples, handedness-specific bridge staples and aptamer/complement or split-aptamer linker strands. TableS2 includes right-handed ds12/ds9 and split-aptamer components, left-handed split components and scrambled control; FigS10 also reports right-handed split sensor. PolyA handles hybridize polyT-coated AuNRs. Materials names p7650 but synthesis says p7560 (visually confirmedp6): exact scaffold unresolved. Native caDNAno is explicitly available from authors upon request, not acquired; no author contact authorized or performed. Core/bridge/linker molar ratio1:1.5:2 does not establish a complete replacement inventory. Full table routing, core geometry and parent design remain pending.'), ('10.1021/acsnano.8b08010', '14005616-nn8b08010_si_001.pdf', '14005616', 'SI sectionsI–III; TablesS1/S2; PDFp4 modified table visually inspected', 'Triangular origami bears peptide handles at A/B/C32 and37, biotin-EGF attachment at A/B/C56, and15 amino anchors at A/B/C5,13,33,42,50. Outer peptide/EGF and inner amino anchors have distinct roles. TableS1 A33-Amino core matches TableS2 C33 rather than A33; C33-Amino differs from its same-named base and resembles a shortened C13 region. Source labels retained; no repair inferred. Full per-variant mapping and scaffold/native parent remain unresolved. Covalent immobilization uses carboxyl-silane nanocavities;300nm versus1micrometer array pitch is substrate patterning, not new DNA core. Six-peptide characterization and binding-density experiments do not prove all variant recipes complete.')]
def main():
 pubs={p['registry_key']:p for p in L.read('publication_reviews')}
